    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i see. so you're saying it's more like a fundamental truth rather than a debate. but some people say that kids are just being influenced by what's popular or that it's something they'll grow out of. if i tell my kid it's \"part of who they are\" like an eye color, am i ignoring the perspective that it might just be a phase or a social thing? shouldn't we present both sides so they can think for themselves?",
